Dial: 5 Crown Games — Privacy Policy
Last updated: November 12, 2026

The short version: Dial does not collect, transmit, or sell any of your data.
The games run entirely on your Apple Watch.

DEVELOPER
Dial is developed by Dzianis Milasheuski, an individual developer based in
Lithuania. Questions about this policy: info@porconova.com

WHAT WE COLLECT
Nothing. Dial has no analytics, no ads, no tracking, no accounts, and no
servers that receive your data. There is no sign-up and no login. We do not
know who you are, which games you play, or how you play them.

HOW THE APP WORKS
- The games run on the watch itself. Nothing is downloaded to play them and
  nothing is uploaded.
- The app stores on the watch, in its own private storage: your best and last
  score in each game, the game you played last (so the menu opens on it), which
  game you chose as your free game, which game tips you have already seen, your
  Haptics and Sound settings, and whether Dial Full is unlocked as last
  confirmed by the App Store, so that games you own do not appear locked for a
  moment at launch.
- This data never leaves the watch through the app. Like other app data, it
  may be included in the backup of your Apple Watch that Apple keeps on your
  paired iPhone; that backup is handled by Apple, not by us.
- The watch-face complication only opens the app. It shows a fixed symbol and
  reads none of your data.
- Sounds are short clips bundled with the app and played on the watch; they
  follow Silent Mode and can be turned off in Settings.
- The app does not use the network for gameplay, and it does not use the
  camera, the microphone, your location, your health data, your contacts, or
  your photos. It does not read any device or advertising identifier.

WHAT LEAVES YOUR DEVICE
Nothing is sent to us, ever. The only communication the app starts is with
Apple's App Store, to show the price of Dial Full, to make a purchase you
confirm, and to check or restore that purchase (see PURCHASES).

PURCHASES
One game of your choice is free forever. Dial Full, which unlocks all five
games, is a one-time, non-recurring In-App Purchase sold through Apple's App
Store. Apple, not the developer, processes payment and handles your Apple
Account. We receive no personal or payment information — only whether this
Apple Account holds a valid Dial Full entitlement, which the app checks with
Apple on the watch using StoreKit. Restore Purchase asks Apple to sync your
purchases; Apple may ask you to sign in. Family Sharing is supported: if a
family organiser shares Dial Full, Apple tells the app that the entitlement
is valid, and nothing about your family group is shared with us.

YOUR RIGHTS
Because the app collects no personal information on the developer's side,
there is no developer-held data for you to access, correct, export, or delete.
Data stored on the watch can be removed by deleting the app, or inside it:
Settings → Reset Scores clears the best and last score of every game. Your
free-game choice stays, because it is part of what you are entitled to. No data
about you is held anywhere else.

CHILDREN
Dial is a set of simple arcade games suitable for all ages. It collects no
data from anyone, including children under the age of 13, and contains no
ads, no links out of the app, and no social features.

REGULATORY NOTES
The app is designed so that no directly identifying personal information
(name, email, IP address, advertising identifier, account ID) is collected by
the developer or by any third party the developer uses. The app contains no
third-party SDKs. Its privacy manifest declares no tracking, no tracking
domains and no collected data types; the only required-reason API it uses is
on-device storage of its own settings (UserDefaults, reason CA92.1). In App
Store terms, the app's privacy label is "Data Not Collected".

CHANGES
If this policy changes, the new version will be published at the same address
with a new date at the top.

